Subject: R1, COSE key validation and the key algorithm
Reason: W3C L3 7.1 step 20 (alg among the offered ones) was not implemented: an unknown alg fell through the switch and registered an unusable key with PHP warnings; every COSE value is now type-checked before use (no strlen()/ord() on null, bools or text), and processCreate() returns credentialAlg (AuthenticatorData::getCredentialPublicKeyAlg()) so the caller checks it against the offered list (audit 2, 3, 9).

